what Twilight scene made you the most  emotional and one moment on set made  Kristen Stewart say I was so  transcendently weird that day number one  there was real magic in the air that day  the wedding scene was the last part  filmed for Breaking Dawn part one and  Kristen Stewart said that she could  really feel the series coming to its end  not only that but being a fan of the  books she said she got oddly emotional  seeing the scene come together I felt  good that day Christian was apparently  so excited that she wanted to run down  the aisle saying that she was literally  pulling away from Billy Burke ready even  Robert Pattinson noticed telling  Entertainment Weekly I could see her  getting sort of emotionally affected by  it and I almost didn't want to stay at  the end of the aisle I wanted to go down  and say stop being so ridiculous  number two we almost didn't get to see  Robert as Edward Twilight director  Catherine Hardwick admitted that she  wasn't entirely sold on Robert when he  arrived at auditions sharing that Rob  walked in and he had his hair dyed black  for some play with these wacky bangs and  I'm like oh okay let's see how this goes  it was Rob's chemistry with Kristen that  changed Hardwick's mind I just want to  try one thing the two played out the  kissing scene on Hardwick's bed and  according to her Rob was so into it he  fell off the bed afterwards Kristen  insisted that Robert be the one to  perform opposite her as Edward and even  hardwood commented I could tell they had  a lot of chemistry so the lion fell in  love with the lamp number three Taylor  Lautner's shirtless scenes weren't  nearly as fun for him as they were for  us especially when it came to filming  his breakup scene in the rain for New  Moon Taylor admitted that he struggled  with the cold playing werewolf Jacob  Black Taylor wasn't allowed to show any  response to the Cold War water he was  drenched with from an onset rain Tower  and although it only took them about  four minutes to film the scene he had to  redo it several times throughout the day  to push through he had to take myself to  another world so during the scene I  wasn't sitting there shivering between  takes he could take advantage of the  onset blankets and heater but only for  about two minutes before he had to  return number four you kind of have to  feel bad for her Kristen Stewart had  food poisoning the day she shot the tent  scene for Eclipse luckily all she really  had to do was lie there shivering anyway  but Stephanie Meyer who was visiting the  set that day revealed that Kristen was  so sick between takes Taylor Lautner  played the hero that day grabbing her a  garbage can in case she needed to throw  up survival 101 the Twilight writer  recalled that everybody was taking care  of her and everything but it was a hard  day she expressed Sympathy For What the  leading lady had to go through saying  that Kristen's job was so hard as she  had to perform shivering all while  feeling like she needed to throw up  number five you might remember this  scene for how intense it got Robert  Pattinson remembers it for different  reasons he revealed in an interview with  the independent the hardest scene to  fill was probably the birth scene in  Breaking Dawn Part One mainly because it  was hilarious and it was supposed to be  really serious he admitted once that a  Comic-Con panel that he thought the  Scene goes very far which might explain  what he found so funny but he also added  that there was no other way to do it  apparently he was laughing so hard that  he couldn't stop tears from falling  adding that it looks like I'm crying in  the thing he might have been able to use  those tears to his Advantage but playing  Edward Cullen he was not supposed to be  able to cry as a vampire number six just  like any family the cullins didn't  always get along Ashley Greene revealed  in an interview with people that there  were plenty of ups and downs and some  drama between the cast on set as she  pointed out five years is a long time to  spend together without any tips though  she'd add that many of the actors had  been in their 20s at the time so you can  imagine who you were in your 20s versus  who you are now although she didn't give  many details one scuffle we are aware of  was between her and Nikki Reed when the  two were reunited on Ashley Greene's  podcast she expressed that Nikki and I  went back and forth where we were cool  and then we didn't want anything to do  with each other and then we were cool  again number seven being a star isn't as  glamorous as you might think Although  our three leads were all close when  filming began Kristen Stewart would  state in an interview that on the  Twilight sets towards the end I found  that people didn't really talk to us  anymore she said that it felt as though  someone had told the rest of the cast to  avoid her unless they had a reason to  approach going on to say it's like now  you are just completely isolating me so  thanks but the worst part about it for  her was that the rest of the cast might  think she was was the one asking to be  left alone which is like do not  represent me ever overall she summarized  the experience by saying that it was  just really annoying number eight they  seemed like good friends while filming  the first Twilight movie it was clear  that Kristen Stewart and Nikki Reed had  grown close with Nikki even sharing that  Kristen and I are best friends yet when  it came time to film Eclipse feelings  had obviously changed while discussing  her co-star Nikki admitted that they had  been close in the beginning but that  success had changed the dynamic we are  not all best friends and we're not all  going to hang out together after the  final movie is done I don't understand  what I did  this statement only fueled fan rumors  that Robert Pattinson had driven a wedge  between the two friends with some even  suggesting that they may have been  involved in an onset love triangle  although Nikki Reed has denied ever  dating Robert Pattinson number nine it  had to end eventually Robert Pattinson  and Christian Stewart shot their final  scene for Breaking Dawn part two  together but it was far from a special  moment rather Robert would later admit  that he felt a little weird getting so  emotional over the end when there was  only the two of them there and then they  just end it and it's like well okay well  that's that he and Kristen been there  awkward goodbyes but both of them knew  that they'd be seeing each other again  only four months later for the press  release Robert went on to say that he  figured the end of their tour would make  for a harder goodbye I'm really really  curious what it's going to be like the  last day of this tour number 10 he  played The Lone Wolf to the end Taylor  Lautner had a hard time letting go of  the Twilight franchise and to make  matters worse he didn't even have a  chance to give a proper goodbye to his  co-stars in an interview Taylor revealed  that my last day of shooting I was by  myself so that was kind of sad although  his second to last day was spent  shooting a scene with Robert Pattinson  and Kristen Stewart he admitted that it  was a little emotional seeing his  co-stars on set for the last time  emphasizing that it was tough for us  because we had been playing these  characters for so long and spending so  much time together for so long the  Twilight franchise was not an easy  filming process which emotional behind  the scenes story surprised you the most  we'd love to hear your opinions so make  them heard down in the comments
 

